  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_5' aria-label=\" Subramani versus State of Karnataka pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('5','2026','2026_3_576_585','2026INSC249'); ><font size='4'> <strong>SUBRAMANI<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>STATE OF KARNATAKA </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 3 S.C.R. 576</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 249</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000902026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PANKAJ MITHAL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SARASA VENKATANARAYANA BHATTI</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the appellant is guilty of the offences u/ss.302 and 498A of IPC and whether the sentence (two years of simple imprisonment along with fine of Rs.2,000/- and in default in payment of the same, with a further three months of simple imprisonment u/s.498A IPC and to him is justified. Headnotes&dagger; Penal Code, 1860 &ndash; ss.302 and 498A &ndash; Allegation against appellant that he poured kerosene on his wife, lit a candle and threw it upon her &ndash; Victim died due to severe burn injuries &ndash; FIR registered u/ss.302 and 498A &ndash; The<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 17-03-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 2432/2010</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('5','2026','2026_3_576_585','2026INSC249','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn bt